,"type":"text"},{"text":"demand. There is no flow when the supplies do not sum to zero or some set of vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"supplies more than its out-edges carry. Costs may be negative, and negative cycles are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"saturated. A self-loop carries its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise. Capacities may be of an unsigned type, up to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int.max"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Computed by the network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Which optimum is returned when several exist is unspecified, but the same input always","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gives the same result. ","type":"text"},{"code":"supply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, then, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each edge in position order, ","type":"text"},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and then ","type":"text"},{"code":"cost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", before any work.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every capacity is at least zero; capacities, supplies and costs fit in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":"; Σ capacity × |cost| fits in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cost"},{"text":" (checked before solving, since it bounds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"total cost); 4(n + 1)(the greatest |cost| of a non-loop edge + 1) fits in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solver’s artificial cost, with room for its potentials and reduced costs); the positive","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"supplies sum within ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Capacity"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows","doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/minimumcostflow(supply:capacity:cost:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A least-cost flow within capacities that meets every supply, or nil when there is none.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumCostFlow","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"supply"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"capacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s: